          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Franklin's multi-sensor design genuinely fixes the two problems that make cheap stud finders frustrating: calibration errors and edge guessing. Within the range, the M210 is the one to buy, because it does everything the famous 710+ does and adds a wire indicator and rechargeable support.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the MAX only for plaster, tile or layered walls, save with the M150 or M50 on plain drywall, and keep a magnet in the same drawer to confirm the reading that matters before you drill.
